WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.925
Unit 3.

2
00:00:00.925 --> 00:00:05.087
The metrics measure protected
coverage, not whether a setting exists.

3
00:00:05.087 --> 00:00:08.563
Client coverage, ninety-eight
percent after ring three.

4
00:00:08.563 --> 00:00:11.612
Sign-ins through the service,
ninety-five percent.

5
00:00:11.612 --> 00:00:15.475
Compliant network enforcement, a
hundred percent after ring three.

6
00:00:15.475 --> 00:00:20.950
The Quick Access residual, and apps
without an assignment or policy, both zero.

7
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.540
The T L S failure share under one percent,

8
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.600
with more than ninety
days of certificate life.

9
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.312
And no table silent for twenty-four hours.

10
00:00:29.312 --> 00:00:30.537
Then the rollback.

11
00:00:30.537 --> 00:00:34.978
In an incident that touches several
steps, reverse newest first:

12
00:00:34.978 --> 00:00:39.501
Conditional Access policies from
Steps 10, 7, 6 and 5 to report-only;

13
00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:42.014
the security profile links removed;

14
00:00:42.014 --> 00:00:45.616
universal tenant restrictions
tagging turned off;

15
00:00:45.616 --> 00:00:51.060
the affected groups removed from the
traffic profiles; the V P N route restored;

16
00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:55.500
and signaling turned off last, only
after no policy depends on it.

17
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.242
Every rollback is a change with a record,

18
00:00:58.242 --> 00:01:03.120
followed by the Step 2.1 export, so
the evidence shows the state after it.
